Vendored third-party dependency
===============================

  Library:  bignum (Noir)
  Upstream: https://github.com/noir-lang/noir-bignum
  Tag:      v0.7.5
  Commit:   4f0b42abed0fe426e816b6d993acdf7b877bf01e
  License:  Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE)

Copied from the tag above (LICENSE, README.md, Nargo.toml, src/). One change:
Nargo.toml's `poseidon` dependency points at Perch's vendored
noir-lang/poseidon v0.2.0 (`vendor/perch/circuits/vendor/poseidon`) instead
of the git tag v0.1.1, so the workspace has one Poseidon library. bignum uses
it only in `derive_from_seed`, which this circuit does not call.

v0.7.5 is the latest release that compiles with nargo 1.0.0-beta.9. Its
`evaluate_quadratic_expression` does not range-check its operands, and
`validate_in_field` proves `x <= p`, not `x < p`; upstream changed both in
v0.11.0 (https://github.com/noir-lang/noir-bignum/pull/270). The RSA module
(`lib/src/rsa.nr`) therefore range-checks every operand and product itself
and proves `signature < modulus` with its own strict comparison.

CHECKSUMS.sha256 pins every vendored file;
`scripts/check-vendor.sh` fails on any drift.
